# Intermediate build output. The CMake trees are machine-specific and full of
# absolute paths; the binaries they produce are committed under bin/ instead.
build/

# The compiled installer. It is nearly a hundred megabytes of the same ROMs
# that are already committed under bin/, and a blob committed once is in every
# clone forever. It is attached to the release it belongs to instead.
dist/
*.obj
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.exp
*.lib
*.user
*.suo
.vs/

# The phone firmware and the binaries are committed, so a clone is a working
# copy rather than something that still needs a 250 MB download and a build.
# Two of the ROM images are over 50 MB; that is a deliberate trade, and it
# cannot be taken back out without rewriting history.
#
# What is not committed is the install-time residue that lands in bin/ when the
# installer is pointed at it: Inno's own uninstaller, and the voice filter the
# installer writes to record the male/female choice.
bin/unins000.*
bin/roms/voices.ini

# Output of tools/verify_port.py, which re-renders every voice with the C++
# engine to diff against the Python one.
samples-cpp/

# The previous project's SAPI wrapper, kept locally for reference.
legacy-bestspeech/

# Python bytecode from the test harnesses
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
